WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
valve. Now the next thing to find are the

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:08.000
semilunar valves. So this is the

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.000
aorta, and you can see that the

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
semilunar valve right here has

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.000
been cut. So blood goes into the left atrium, left

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.000
AV valve, up through the aortic semilunar

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.000
valve, and then to the whole

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.000
body.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Okay, and then the pulmonary trunk

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.000
also has a semilunar valve, and you can

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:39.000
see it just by peeking right down in

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.000
there. Okay.
